I see exactly what is causing the layout to break in the image. The DateTimePicker container is overflowing horizontally for two cascading reasons:
 1. **The Box Model Collision:** The wrapping <Box> has p: 3 (padding) but lacks boxSizing: "border-box". In standard CSS, padding is added *on top* of the 100% width, pushing it outside the parent container.
 2. **Helper Text Stretching:** The helperText string is quite long. By default, MUI might try to render it on a single line, which forces the TextField to stretch horizontally to accommodate the text, completely ignoring the parent container's bounds.
To fix this, we need to enforce strict CSS boundaries on the wrapper box and force the helper text to wrap properly.
### The Fix
Replace your current scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE" block with this updated version. I have added responsive padding, strict width controls, and a targeted CSS override for the helper text.
```jsx
{scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE" && (
  <LocalizationProvider dateAdapter={AdapterDayjs}>
    <Box
      sx={{
        mt: 2,
        mb: 2,
        p: { xs: 2, sm: 3 }, // Responsive padding to fit nicely on smaller screens
        borderRadius: 2,
        border: "1px solid",
        borderColor: "divider",
        animation: "fadeIn 0.2s ease-in-out",
        backgroundColor: "white",
        width: "100%",
        boxSizing: "border-box", // CRITICAL: Ensures padding is calculated inside the 100% width
      }}
    >
      <DateTimePicker
        label="New Execution Date & Time"
        value={finalScheduleTime ? dayjs(finalScheduleTime) : null}
        onChange={(newValue) => {
          setFinalScheduleTime(newValue ? newValue.format("YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm") : "");
        }}
        minDateTime={dayjs().add(30, 'minute')}
        maxDateTime={dayjs().add(24, 'hour')}
        timeSteps={{ minutes: 1 }}
        slotProps={{
          textField: {
            size: 'small',
            fullWidth: true,
            required: true,
            sx: { 
              caretColor: 'transparent',
              // CRITICAL: Force the helper text to wrap to the next line instead of stretching the parent
              '& .MuiFormHelperText-root': {
                whiteSpace: 'normal',
                wordBreak: 'break-word',
                marginInline: 0, // Aligns the text perfectly flush with the input border
                mt: 1
              }
            },
            helperText: "Scheduling is only allowed between 30 minutes and 24 hours from current time.",
            onKeyDown: (e) => e.preventDefault(),
            onPaste: (e) => e.preventDefault(),
            inputProps: { readOnly: true } 
          }
        }}
      />
    </Box>
  </LocalizationProvider>
)}

```
### Why this works:
 * **boxSizing: "border-box"**: This tells the browser to include the padding and border within the element's total width and height. Now, width: "100%" means it will perfectly hug the inside of the grid above it without spilling over.
 * **whiteSpace: 'normal' & wordBreak: 'break-word'**: These specific CSS injections into the MuiFormHelperText-root class force the long warning text to gracefully break onto a second line instead of pushing the calendar input field off the screen.
